    "updated_at": "2019-12-28T16:10:04Z",
    "body": "I just checked across some of my old themes from the zprezto suite: every one of them behaves the way we do (with continued error status until a new command is entered).\r\n\r\nI don't know how alien-minimal is accomplishing updating the exit status, because their code is a bit hard for them to read (not their fault--almost all sufficiently complex shell prompts become hard to read for a newcomer). It might be interesting to potentially update to use their technique, but we would need to make sure it also extends to work in other shells as well, since we want to minimize incompatible behavior between shells.",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
