    "body": "Hi, I just wanted to elaborate on a similar behavior i found (using bash):\r\nwhen tab-completing starship.rs copies the state, and time it took to execute the last command:\r\n![Screenshot from 2021-02-12 09-50-00](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/46485458/107747513-cf07c380-6d17-11eb-91c4-ed92c4e7663e.png)\r\n\r\nI `tail -f /dev/null` for 13 seconds, then I immediately `ls asd` and attempt tab-completion. it's a minor thing, but it make it appear like the tab-completion took a looong time. I expect tab-completion to not have a state nor time. (double-pressing esc, bringing up `Display all <N> possibilities (y or n)` also is reported this way)",
